@@ -0,0 +1,6 @@
+{
+  "file": "src/flows.ts",
+  "snippet": "tags: z.string().describe('Up to three lowercase topic tags, comma separated'),",
+  "cause": "The TicketSummarySchema declares `tags` as a single string and its description asks the model for comma-separated text, so the structured output comes back as \"shipping, damage\" instead of an array of tags.",
+  "evidence": "src/flows.ts:8 defines `tags: z.string()` with the description 'Up to three lowercase topic tags, comma separated', and summarizeTicket (src/flows.ts:12-25) uses this schema as its output schema, so the model is constrained to return one string. Changing it to z.array(z.string()) makes the output schema match the list the dashboard expects; `npx tsc --noEmit` passes. I did not run the flow against the model, since that needs live model access."
+}
